      "message": "We might be able to remove that in a separate patch, since it\u0027s just an interface that gets set by each provider. I do think that in a subsequent patch, we will want to remove this logic in favor of having custom providers handle the storage bits if they need it. That way the manager doesn\u0027t need a hook to check persistence properties of the provider being used.\n\nAll in all, yes I think we can remove this hook. All take a shot at refactoring those interfaces in a subsequent patch.",
